From dec7bb6303f98cac1bdba69b4e778378877571dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fmillion <47171880+fmillion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:15:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] platform/x86: intel: ishtp_eclite: Support Lakefield
 (INT3538) ECLite

Lakefield firmware (e.g. Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Fold Gen 1) describes the
ECLite device as _HID INT3538 rather than INTC1035, with the same
command (0x9F) and data (0x9E) operation regions. Without a match the
driver fails with "eclite ACPI device not found" and every
ECLite-backed ACPI method (battery, AC, lid, keyboard dock state) is
non-functional.

The Fold's data region is also 0x1A8 bytes and its battery methods read
beyond the driver's 384-byte limit (e.g. 16 bytes at 0x186), which made
_BIF/_BIX fail with -EINVAL. The message header encodes offset and
length in 9 bits, so size the shadow buffer to the full 512-byte space.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/intel/ishtp_eclite.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/ishtp_eclite.c b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/ishtp_eclite.c
index bca7e2178..62a894662 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/ishtp_eclite.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/ishtp_eclite.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 #define ECL_CL_RX_RING_SIZE	16
 #define ECL_CL_TX_RING_SIZE	8
 
-#define ECL_DATA_OPR_BUFLEN	384
+#define ECL_DATA_OPR_BUFLEN	512	/* 9-bit offset/length in ecl_message_header */
 #define ECL_EVENTS_NOTIFY	333
 
 #define cmd_opr_offsetof(element)	offsetof(struct opregion_cmd, element)
@@ -290,6 +290,8 @@ static int acpi_find_eclite_device(struct ishtp_opregion_dev *opr_dev)
 
 	/* Find ECLite device and save reference */
 	adev = acpi_dev_get_first_match_dev("INTC1035", NULL, -1);
+	if (!adev)	/* Lakefield platforms (e.g. ThinkPad X1 Fold Gen 1) */
+		adev = acpi_dev_get_first_match_dev("INT3538", NULL, -1);
 	if (!adev) {
 		dev_err(cl_data_to_dev(opr_dev), "eclite ACPI device not found\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
-- 
